{
  "case_id": "2009-09-158",
  "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: 2244 doesn't make any reference to judgment, 2244(b). And now you bring in the concept of a judgment by looking at another provision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You, Billy Joe Magwood, are guilty and sentenced to death by electrocution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State's proposed rule is if a claim could have been or was raised in a prior petition, it is barred by Section 2244 (2) or (1)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, how -- how does the State's definition at page 17 of the red brief not comport with the whole idea of second or successive?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what the State is asking for is a brandnew waiver system that has never been imposed in any decision from this Court and there have been three decisions from this Court where it would have come up. One is Burton, another is Richmond, which is cited in our brief, and the third case is -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, wait. First -\u00ad before you get off whether this is second or successive, although the -- the State didn't put it this way, I think what the State is clearly saying is that if it is the second petition that could have raised this issue, it is second or successive. What's wrong with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And Mr. Fisher uses the word \"claim\" as -- differently."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "f7461f774c4aa36f9c7e4611528db2ad4a5680f1036c7fbaa21e7559cadab58a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7461f774c4a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MAZE: Yes. And again, the reason is -\u00ad it's just like you said in Espinoza yesterday -- you get one full and fair opportunity to litigate a claim. If you raise the claim in the first petition, it's not abusive, as this Court said it in McCleskey, because McCleskey says it is only abusive if you could have but didn't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-09-158",
      "confidence": 0.0,
